{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggV7JLCrJL9zDvkPwaQx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ligand-field model cannot give Dq or B for this species, so I am not reporting values for them.\n\n**Why:** Vanadate contains V(V), which is d⁰ (3d⁰). With no d electrons there are no d–d (ligand-field) transitions, so there are no ¹E, ³T₁ or similar excited states whose energies depend on Dq and B. The Racah parameter B measures inter-electron repulsion among d electrons, which is absent here.\n\n**What the bands are:** The three intense bands (ε ≈ 2 740–9 580 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹) are ligand-to-metal charge-transfer (LMCT) transitions. They move electron density from O 2p orbitals of the tetrahedral VO₄³⁻ anion into the empty V 3d orbitals. Their energies are set by the V–O electronegativity difference and orbital overlap, not by a ligand-field splitting of a d-shell. Fitting them to Dq and B would be meaningless.\n\n**What would be needed:** Values of Dq and B require d–d bands from a partially filled d-shell (for example V(IV), d¹, or V(III), d²), or a separate analysis that models the charge-transfer manifold explicitly.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"VO4^3- is a d0 V(V) complex whose observed bands are O→V charge-transfer transitions, not d–d transitions, so Dq and B cannot be determined in the ligand-field model.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc3cb449-3d10-4f92-aa62-5df4cb7c4756","uuid":"250e1561-20f2-494a-a8f3-e2bba60c2c76","timestamp":"